  "notes": "HUD Command Center aesthetic for vietnamtrainingpilot portfolio. Design system emphasizes: (1) Precision: Type scales use specific tracking/leading for readability at all sizes; spacing follows 4px grid for consistency. (2) Visual Hierarchy: Accent uses cool blues (#0066cc, #4d94ff) paired with cyan accent-2 (#00b8e6, #00d4ff) for tech authenticity without neon overreach. Status colors (success/warning/error) are muted in light mode, vibrant but purposeful in dark mode. (3) HUD Flavor: Shadows include 'hudGlow' variants for optional accent borders and subtle insets; motion curves use 'reveal' (1.56 cubic-bezier peak) for UI pop, 'snap' for quick responses. (4) Accessibility: Contrast ratios meet WCAG AA in both modes; dark mode uses increased saturation on secondaries to maintain readability. (5) Avoids: Flat unstyled defaults (fonts, weights, and leading are prescribed); generic purple-gradient SaaS tropes (no gradients, intent-clear color roles); overdone sci-fi clichés (no neon, no hard glows, no excessive line effects). Font family assumed to be system sans-serif or Inter/Geist in implementation."
